      "card_ids": ["C03"],
      "claim": "The CB2 tracer [11C]MA2 showed high brain uptake in mice, supporting good BBB penetration.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C06"],
      "claim": "Compounds 5i/5o achieved greatly improved brain/plasma ratios (~10) and were not susceptible to P-glycoprotein-mediated efflux.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C04"],
      "claim": "A structurally related glycerol derivative showed enhanced BBB permeability with measurable brain concentrations after oral dosing in rats.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "All high-transfer experimental analogues demonstrate meaningful in vivo brain penetration, including structurally related triazolopyrazines with brain concentrations far exceeding plasma-free levels; therefore the query is predicted to have meaningful CNS access.",
